<title>INDIA: India's NSE puts circuit breaker on six top stocks.</title>
<headline>India's NSE puts circuit breaker on six top stocks.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's National Stock Exchange (NSE) on Wednesday put a circuit breaker on six leading stocks after their prices fell seven percent, traders said.</p>
<p>NSE said a circuit breaker was activated on Hindustan Lever, Bajaj Auto, ACC, TELCO, Gujarat Ambuja Cements and Raymond, after these shares fell sharply.  </p>
<p>Auto and cement stocks took a beating on the NSE and the Bombay bourse.</p>
<p>Bombay's benchmark stocks index fell 81.23 points or 2.8 percent to 2867 at mid-session.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
